{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790947897,"nonce":"+v9g9YgY1OVuT4aKcRW083V1ArI=","message":"**Owner's ruling (2026-10-02, revised): the approval grant is given and taken by a CLI subcommand only. ⛔ The previous comment (declarative config) is superseded. Do not build from it.**\n\n**The decision.** `oto grant` and `oto revoke` are subcommands, like `oto bootstrap` (`internal/app/bootstrap.go`) and reset-password. Running one requires a shell on the host and the database credentials, which is the authority that could write the rows by hand anyway. That answers bootstrap: the first grant and every later one come from the same place. There is **no in-app grant or revoke**, so the HTTP API and UI show grants **read-only**. This matters for double approval (ADR 0054 §4): one holder cannot mint a second approver (an alt account) from inside oto. Following bootstrap's own argument, no HTTP route may ever create a grant.\n\n**Shape.**\n- A grant is a row `(org, ToolServer, user)`, created by `oto grant remedy-approver --org \u003cslug\u003e --toolserver \u003cname\u003e --email \u003caddr\u003e` and removed by `oto revoke …`. The row records who ran it (the CLI as actor) and when, using the app-owned clock.\n- The user is resolved by email, so a shadow member (no address, migration 00074) can never hold a grant. A disabled user's grant stops counting.\n- The ToolServer must exist when the grant is made. Deleting a ToolServer deletes its grants.\n- The grant is a permission only. It routes nothing, notifies no one and creates no queue (H-1).\n- ADR 0054 §4 is amended to record this.\n\n**Done when.** `oto grant` / `oto revoke` exist and are tested; the API and UI list a ToolServer's grant holders read-only; no HTTP route writes a grant (asserted by a test over the route table, if the repo has that pattern); an approval by a non-holder is refused with a typed error; tests cover a holder, a non-holder, a revoked holder, a disabled user, a shadow member and an unknown ToolServer.\n\n**Mode.** AFK.","files":null}]}